1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:04,650
Where should Architectural
Intelligence actually execute?

2
00:00:04,920 --> 00:00:08,380
That's the question I've reached
while building the conceptual

3
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:10,650
architecture for the Knowledge API.

4
00:00:10,720 --> 00:00:13,590
Hello I'm Russell and
welcome to episode 10 of

5
00:00:13,670 --> 00:00:16,640
the Articulate Journal where
I'm exploring what it takes

6
00:00:16,720 --> 00:00:19,940
to build an AI-native architecture
from the first principles.

7
00:00:20,050 --> 00:00:24,545
Over the past few episodes
we've explored the Knowledge

8
00:00:24,625 --> 00:00:27,930
Model. looked at how AI can
reason over architectural

9
00:00:27,970 --> 00:00:32,630
knowledge and how we can
describe a capability behaviour

10
00:00:32,710 --> 00:00:37,070
using DCL. Every architecture
eventually reaches a point where

11
00:00:37,110 --> 00:00:38,830
the ideas have to become software.

12
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:42,150
For Articulate I want
that point to arrive very

13
00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:46,330
soon. Architectural Intelligence
won't simply answer prompts.

14
00:00:46,410 --> 00:00:50,600
It will retrieve knowledge, reason
over architectural problems, invoke

15
00:00:50,680 --> 00:00:54,960
tools, collaborate with people,
evolve the Knowledge Model and

16
00:00:55,040 --> 00:00:58,600
coordinate long running work.
Something has to orchestrate all

17
00:00:58,670 --> 00:01:02,440
of that. In other words
Articulate needs a runtime.

18
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:06,200
At first glance it seemed like
a straightforward technology

19
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:10,147
decision. Should I use Dapr,
Temporal, LangGraph or Microsoft

20
00:01:10,227 --> 00:01:15,620
Agent Framework? There are already
several excellent technologies available

21
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:18,380
so perhaps the obvious
next step is simply to

22
00:01:18,460 --> 00:01:21,340
compare them. The more
I thought about it the

23
00:01:21,380 --> 00:01:23,890
more I realized I wasn't
actually ready to compare

24
00:01:24,010 --> 00:01:26,460
any of them because I
still hadn't answered the

25
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:31,520
simpler question. What is the
runtime actually responsible for?

26
00:01:32,130 --> 00:01:35,190
That question completely changed
how I approached the decision.

27
00:01:35,230 --> 00:01:38,430
Instead of looking at products
I started looking back

28
00:01:38,510 --> 00:01:42,400
at the architecture we'd already
defined and something interesting

29
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:47,810
happened. The architecture had
already begun answering the question.

30
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:52,780
Articulate isn't a traditional
request response application.

31
00:01:53,650 --> 00:01:58,060
Architectural reasoning may take
minutes, hours and even days.

32
00:01:58,610 --> 00:02:02,140
The capability may need to
retrieve knowledge from several

33
00:02:02,220 --> 00:02:05,050
software sources before
it can reach a conclusion.

34
00:02:05,190 --> 00:02:07,850
It may invoke external tools.

35
00:02:08,090 --> 00:02:11,740
It may collaborate with other
specialised capabilities.

36
00:02:11,810 --> 00:02:15,370
It may need clarification
from a human architect before

37
00:02:15,450 --> 00:02:18,840
it can continue. And when
something goes wrong it

38
00:02:18,920 --> 00:02:21,450
shouldn't simply lose
everything and start again.

39
00:02:21,580 --> 00:02:25,480
Without deliberately planning it
the previous episodes had already

40
00:02:25,560 --> 00:02:28,690
revealed a set of responsibilities
that any runtime would

41
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:32,010
need to support. It would need
to coordinate long-running

42
00:02:32,090 --> 00:02:35,680
work. It should orchestrate
specialised capabilities.

43
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:37,530
It should invoke external tools.

44
00:02:37,640 --> 00:02:41,300
It should recover safely
from failure and it should

45
00:02:41,340 --> 00:02:43,790
provide visibility into what is going on.

46
00:02:43,950 --> 00:02:47,600
And it should remain flexible
enough to evolve alongside

47
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:51,060
